<title>USA: CBOT May volume falls 4.0 pct yr/yr to 19.85 mln.</title>
<headline>CBOT May volume falls 4.0 pct yr/yr to 19.85 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said trading volume in its futures and options totaled 19,852,913 contracts in May, down 4.0 percent from 20,687,991 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for May 1997 and percentage change followed by May 1996 volume:</p>
<p>All futures     16,066,193     - 0.3     16,109,939</p>
<p>  Agricultural   4,112,872     -11.4	4,640,764</p>
<p>  Financial     11,947,361     + 4.2     11,460,703</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   3,786,720     -17.3	4,578,052</p>
<p>  Agricultural   1,100,161     -21.9	1,408,772</p>
<p>  Financial	2,685,945     -15.2	3,168,547</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     8,339,072     + 5.1	7,932,273</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 2,025,603     - 8.4	2,211,270</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes  1,190,565     + 4.9	1,135,475</p>
<p>  Wheat		422,935     -20.5	  531,979</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,291,661     -38.1	2,085,183</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,391,096     +21.0	1,149,340</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    581,886     +32.5	  439,212</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     389,741     + 3.5	  376,716</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,123,848     - 4.5	2,222,764</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   346,443     -52.6	  731,128</p>
<p>  Corn		 330,479     -51.6	  683,164</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   497,034     +22.6	  405,304</p>
<p>((DerivativesDesk 312-408-8750/Email:derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
